91
02:19:40,139 --> 02:19:45,944
It was a tiny red hovel on upper Jerome, a bit run down and rough around the edges.

92
02:19:46,687 --> 02:20:10,295
And Mr. Henry seemed so old to us, even then, with a lot of whiskers, impatient and a little scary. One would suspect that he didn't even like kids, but he really must have loved us. Or else, where did all that penny candy come from? He had all of it. No, seriously.

93
02:20:10,970 --> 02:20:22,175
We'd bust in there with a few nickels or a handful of pennies, all loud and unruly. He'd hush us up while he finished with grown folks' business.

94
02:20:23,221 --> 02:20:51,335
Then he'd be back like a black Willy Wonka up in that old shack. He'd peer over those old horn-rimmed glasses and tell us he didn't have all day. Then he'd blow open one of those small brown kraft paper bags and get to stuffing while we were oohing and aahing and huffing and puffing. See, Mr. Henry had all the treats, all of our favorites, a hundred great sweets.

95
02:20:52,499 --> 02:21:12,327
Root beer barrels and pixie sticks. Squirrel nut zippers and banana splits. Green mint juleps and button strips. Red licorice ropes and bottle nips. He has bazooka Joe bubblegum. And a tiny sucker called the dum-dum. Jawbreakers and tootsie rolls. Sugary love for little kid souls.

96
02:21:13,188 --> 02:21:40,829
Candy necklaces to wear and fight, and waxy red lips with such a sight. Fat gum cigars and kids' cigarettes, right beside the crunchy six-lets. Mary Jane chewies and BB bats, hot fireballs and Mexican hats. Just the genuine Hershey's kisses, all the hits and none of the misses. Like kids' taffy squares and Necco wafers, liquor made in Boston baked beans, gold rocks,

97
02:21:41,605 --> 02:22:06,935
gum in a bag, a kid's idea of sweet tooth swag. Before the days of Laffy Taffys, we would gobble up peppermint patties. Before we knew about gummy bears, Twizzlers always came in pairs. Chewy cow tails had a creamy filling, but sugar babies had top billing. Reese's peanut butter cups had us squealing like newborn pups.

98
02:22:07,559 --> 02:22:27,522
Mike and Iks and orange slices. Saltwater taffy and tiny prices. Lifesavers and charms and fruity flavors. We grabbed those bags like party favors. Chuckles were a favorite choice, and milk dust made us all rejoice. Jolly ranchers and bitter honey, we always got a lot

99
02:22:29,446 --> 02:22:44,701
